(9194, 32282, 'wb_custom_tabs', 'a:6:{i:0;a:6:{s:5:\"title\";s:8:\"BENEFITS\";s:7:\"content\";s:2488:\"<strong>Glycerin:</strong>\r\nGlycerin is a highly effective humectant, meaning it draws moisture from the environment into the skin. This helps to hydrate the skin by maintaining its moisture balance, leaving it feeling soft and supple. Glycerin is also non-comedogenic, making it suitable for all skin types, including sensitive and acne-prone skin. Its ability to improve skin hydration can also enhance the skin’s natural barrier function, reducing the risk of moisture loss and protecting against environmental aggressors.\r\n\r\n<strong>Aloe Barbadensis Leaf Extract:</strong>\r\nAloe vera extract is renowned for its soothing and healing properties. It contains various vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants that help to calm inflammation, reduce redness, and promote skin regeneration. Its hydrating properties make it beneficial for dry or sunburned skin, while its gentle nature makes it suitable for sensitive skin types. Aloe vera also has antimicrobial properties, which can help to prevent infections and support overall skin health.\r\n\r\n<strong>Allantoin:</strong>\r\nAllantoin is a naturally occurring compound found in plants like comfrey and chamomile. It has excellent moisturizing properties and helps to soften and smooth the skin’s texture. Allantoin is also known for its ability to promote wound healing and cell regeneration, making it beneficial for treating minor cuts, burns, and irritations. Additionally, it has anti-inflammatory properties that help to reduce redness and irritation, making it suitable for sensitive or reactive skin.\r\n\r\n<strong>Tocopheryl Acetate:</strong>\r\nTocopheryl acetate is a stable form of vitamin E, a powerful antioxidant that protects the skin from damage caused by free radicals and environmental stressors such as UV radiation and pollution. It helps to strengthen the skin’s barrier function, reducing moisture loss and improving overall hydration. Tocopheryl acetate also has anti-inflammatory properties, which can help to soothe and calm irritated skin, making it particularly beneficial for those with sensitive or sun-damaged skin.\r\n\r\n<strong>Silica:</strong>\r\nSilica is a mineral that is often used in skincare products for its absorbent properties. It helps to absorb excess oil and sebum on the skin’s surface, giving it a mattifying effect and reducing shine. Silica also has a soft-focus effect, helping to blur the appearance of fine lines, wrinkles, and imperfections, giving the skin a smoother and more even texture.\";s:8:\"tab_type\";s:5:\"local\";s:8:\"position\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"nickname\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"slug\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:6:{s:5:\"title\";s:44:\"WHY DO I NEED TO PROTECT MY SKIN EVERY DAY ?\";s:7:\"content\";s:1290:\"Ultraviolet light is invisible to humans, because it has shorter wave lengths than the light we can see. Within the UV spectrum, there are two types of rays that can damage the DNA in your skin cells and lead to skin cancer. It’s important to protect your skin from both types:\r\n– UVB rays cause sunburn and play a key role in developing skin cancer. A sunscreen’s SPF number refers mainly to the amount of UVB protection it provides.\r\n– UVA rays cause skin damage that leads to tanning as well as skin aging, wrinkles and hyperpigmentation. The shortest wavelengths of UVA rays also contribute to sunburn.\r\nIt’s important to look for the words “broad spectrum” on a product’s label, which means it has ingredients that can protect you from UVA as well as UVB rays.\r\nSunscreen should be applied every day, even if it is overcast outside or even if you’re spending the day inside. UV radiation is not only present on a warm summer day but is also present and can damage skin when the weather is cool or cloudy. This is especially the case for people with a fair skin tone, as they have less of the protective pigment called melanin.\r\nHowever, people of all skin tones are subject to skin cancer, and should practice proper sun protection, including wearing daily sunscreen.\";s:8:\"tab_type\";s:5:\"local\";s:8:\"position\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"nickname\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"slug\";s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:6:{s:5:\"title\";s:34:\"THE UV FILTERS USES IN OUR FORMULA\";s:7:\"content\";s:568:\"High Protection chemical Filters blocking the UV rays responsible for photo-aging and sunburn:\r\nEthylhexyl Methoxycinnamate: Also known as Octinoxate, this ingredient provides UVB protection.\r\nButyl Methoxydibenzoylmethane: Also known as Avobenzone, this ingredient absorbs UVA rays.\r\nEthylhexyl Triazone: This is a newer generation UV filter that provides broad-spectrum UVB and short UVA protection.\r\nMethylene Bis-Benzotriazolyl Tetramethylbutylphenol [Nano]: Also known as Tinosorb M, this is a broad-spectrum UV filter that protects against both UVA and UVB rays.\";s:8:\"tab_type\";s:5:\"local\";s:8:\"position\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"nickname\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"slug\";s:0:\"\";}i:3;a:6:{s:5:\"title\";s:26:\"HOW TO APPLY MY SUN CREAM?\";s:7:\"content\";s:341:\"Before exposure, apply enough to cover the exposed area (face and neck). Reapply frequently and especially after bathing and toweling or perspiring. Reducing the amount of sunscreen product applied leads to a significant reduction in protection. Even well protected, reduce exposure as much as possible. Avoid contact with eyes and clothing.\";s:8:\"tab_type\";s:5:\"local\";s:8:\"position\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"nickname\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"slug\";s:0:\"\";}i:4;a:6:{s:5:\"title\";s:30:\"WHAT DOES THE SPF NUMBER MEAN?\";s:7:\"content\";s:288:\"The SPF number tells you how long the sun’s UV radiation would take to redden your skin when using the product exactly as directed versus the amount of time without any sunscreen. So ideally, with SPF 50 it would take you 50 times longer to burn than if you weren’t wearing sunscreen.\";s:8:\"tab_type\";s:5:\"local\";s:8:\"position\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"nickname\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"slug\";s:0:\"\";}i:5;a:6:{s:5:\"title\";s:4:\"INCI\";s:7:\"content\";s:640:\"AQUA (WATER), GLYCERIN, DICAPRYLYL CARBONATE, ETHYLHEXYL METHOXYCINNAMATE, BUTYL METHOXYDIBENZOYLMETHANE, ETHYLHEXYL TRIAZONE, CETEARYL ALCOHOL, METHYLENE BIS-BENZOTRIAZOLYL TETRAMETHYLBUTYLPHENOL [NANO], CETEARETH-25, HYDROGENATED POLYDECENE, OCTOCRYLENE, CETEARETH-6, POTASSIUM CETYL PHOSPHATE, DIMETHICONE, ORYZA SATIVA (RICE) STARCH, CI 77891 (TITANIUM DIOXIDE), GLYCERYL STEARATE, PEG-100 STEARATE, MAGNESIUM ALUMINUM SILICATE, PHENETHYL ALCOHOL, STEARYL ALCOHOL, DECYL GLUCOSIDE, TOCOPHERYL ACETATE, ALOE BARBADENSIS LEAF EXTRACT, XANTHAN GUM, ALLANTOIN, DISODIUM EDTA, POTASSIUM SORBATE, ETHYLHEXYLGLYCERIN, PROPYLENE GLYCOL, SILICA.\";s:8:\"tab_type\";s:5:\"local\";s:8:\"position\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"nickname\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"slug\";s:0:\"\";}}'),
